{
  "name": "How to Plan Your Kitchen for Easy Appliance Access",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Planning an accessible kitchen can make a huge difference in daily life, especially if you or someone in your home has mobility needs. It's all about making sure you can get to and use your appliances comfortably and safely. Here's a quick run-through of how you can approach it. Step 1: Measure your reach. Think about how far you can comfortably reach from a seated or standing position, and plan to place your most-used appliances and items within those easy-to-reach zones. Step 2: Clear pathways. Make sure you have enough clear floor space and circulation paths around appliances so you can move freely without bumping into things or struggling to turn. Step 3: Prioritize placement. Heavy or frequently used items should be at accessible heights to reduce bending and stretching. Step 4: Ensure clearance. Double-check that you can approach, operate, and leave the appliance area without any obstructions. This often means making sure cabinet depths, appliance dimensions, and turning radiuses are all coordinated. When you're dealing with specific mobility challenges, bringing in a professional like HH Remodeling LLC can be really beneficial. We can help integrate all these elements into a functional and safe design. Call us at 303-505-0866 to start planning.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
